# Cloud-role scheduled GRIB fetch (ticket B1 design 6) -- append to
# `crontab -e` on the cloud VM (STINGRAY_ROLE=cloud only; the vessel role
# never runs these, see api/weather_sync.py instead). Cadences match the
# real, confirmed-live cadences from ticket 0.5: NOMADS hourly-ish, ECMWF
# 3-hourly.
#
# Requires the `ingest` extras (cfgrib/eccodes) installed separately from
# the PyInstaller-built `stingray` binary -- ingest/ is a normal Python
# package invocation (`python3 -m ingest.fetch_grib_*`), not bundled into
# the frozen binary (deploy/pyinstaller.spec explicitly excludes cfgrib/
# xarray/h5netcdf/h5py -- see that file's `excludes` list and comment).
#
# 0 * * * *    fetch every hour on the hour
# 5 */3 * * *  fetch every 3 hours, 5 minutes past
#
# Ticket R1: this is the single-pack (Med-only) form, correct for every
# deployment today. Once STINGRAY_REGION_PACKS_PATH is set (multiple
# configured packs, e.g. Med + UK South-West -- see
# docs/region-pack-runbook.md), replace both lines below with
# `ingest.fetch_all_packs --packs-manifest <path> --source nomads|ecmwf`
# instead -- one thin wrapper looping the same two fetchers over every
# pack the manifest lists, so cron never needs editing again when a pack
# is added. See deploy/README.md's "Multi-pack deployments" note.

0 * * * *   cd /opt/stingray-ingest && /opt/stingray-ingest/venv/bin/python3 -m ingest.fetch_grib_nomads --out /opt/stingray/data/weather/nomads_western_med.npz >> /var/log/stingray-fetch-nomads.log 2>&1
5 */3 * * * cd /opt/stingray-ingest && /opt/stingray-ingest/venv/bin/python3 -m ingest.fetch_grib_ecmwf --out /opt/stingray/data/weather/ecmwf_western_med.npz >> /var/log/stingray-fetch-ecmwf.log 2>&1
